/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T165618-008-wcap/assets/20261013T165618-008-wcap/jurisdiction_noridian_dme_mac_jadme.html) | Map code: `JURIS-DME-A` $\\to$ `https://med.noridianmedicare.com/web/jadme`, `JURIS-DME-B` $\\to$ `https://www.cgsmedicare.com/jb/`, `JURIS-DME-C` $\\to$ `https://www.cgsmedicare.com/jc/`, `JURIS-DME-D` $\\to$ `https://med.noridianmedicare.com/web/jddme` |\n| **`HCPCSCode`** | `HCPCS-A6522`, `HCPCS-A6520`, `HCPCS-Q2052` | **Missing (null)** | `https://www.cms.gov/medicare/payment/fee-schedules/dmepos` and `https://clinicaltables.nlm.nih.gov/api/hcpcs/v3/search?terms=A6522` | `HTTP/2 200 OK` (CMS DMEPOS: 217,370 bytes; NLM API: 60 bytes) | [`hcpcs_cms_dmepos_fee_schedule.html`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T165618-008-wcap/assets/20261013T165618-008-wcap/hcpcs_cms_dmepos_fee_schedule.html), [`hcpcs_nlm_search_a6522.json`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T165618-008-wcap/assets/20261013T165618-008-wcap/hcpcs_nlm_search_a6522.json), [`hcpcs_nlm_search_q2052.json`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T165618-008-wcap/assets/20261013T165618-008-wcap/hcpcs_nlm_search_q2052.json) | `https://www.cms.gov/medicare/payment/fee-schedules/dmepos` |\n| **`ICD10Code`** | `ICD10-I97.2`, `ICD10-I89.0`, `ICD10-D80.0` | **Missing (null)** | `https://icd10cmtool.cdc.gov/` and `https://clinicaltables.nlm.nih.gov/api/icd10cm/v3/search?terms=I97.2` | `HTTP/1.1 200 OK` (CDC tool: 730 bytes; NLM API: 67 bytes) | [`icd10_cdc_browser_tool.html`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T165618-008-wcap/assets/20261013T165618-008-wcap/icd10_cdc_browser_tool.html), [`icd10_nlm_search_i972.json`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T165618-008-wcap/assets/20261013T165618-008-wcap/icd10_nlm_search_i972.json), [`icd10_nlm_search_i890.json`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T165618-008-wcap/assets/20261013T165618-008-wcap/icd10_nlm_search_i890.json) | `https://icd10cmtool.cdc.gov/` |\n| **`LobbyingFiling`** | `LDA-c8697fc5-7f3b-4861-8a49-d9e6357ad287` | Hardcoded search homepage | `https://lda.gov/filings/public/filing/c8697fc5-7f3b-4861-8a49-d9e6357ad287/print/` and `https://lda.gov/system/public/` | `HTTP/1.1 200 OK` (Content-Length: 20,953) | [`lobbying_filing_sopr_lda_c8697fc5.html`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T165618-008-wcap/assets/20261013T165618-008-wcap/lobbying_filing_sopr_lda_c8697fc5.html) | `https://lda.gov/filings/public/filing/${filingUuid}/print/` (or `https://lda.gov/system/public/` fallback) |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Explicit Deficiency Register\n\nIn strict adherence to `INV-ABSENCE-01`, this register details every specced requirement in `functional_specification_006.md` that cannot be satisfied by existing codebase components or reachable external endpoints. Zero components or endpoints have been invented:\n\n| Deficiency ID | Specced Requirement / Behavioral Contract | Existing Codebase State | Exact Gap Description \u0026 System Impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **DEF-01** | Removal of Physics Toggle Button (`functional_specification_006.md` Section 3, Section 4.1.1, Acceptance Criteria 1) | `FilterToolbar.tsx` lines 106-122 contains a manual physics toggle button: `{physicsFrozen ? '▶ RESUME PHYSICS' : '⏸ FREEZE PHYSICS'}`. `GraphSyncContext.tsx` maintains `physicsFrozen` state and `togglePhysicsFrozen` callback. | Clutters the top navigation toolbar; forces users to manually intervene in physics rather than allowing forces to settle autonomously. |\n| **DEF-02** | Collapsible Blueprint HUD Accordion (`functional_specification_006.md` Section 3, Section 4.2.1-4.2.3, Acceptance Criteria 2) | `GraphCanvas.tsx` lines 469-497 renders a fixed, static HUD panel at `top: 14, left: 14` with `pointerEvents: 'none'`. | Panel cannot be collapsed or clicked. On standard and smaller screen viewports, the fixed telemetry panel collides and visually overlaps with top toolbar dropdowns (\"JURISDICTION\", \"POLICY\", \"GRAPHRAG CHAT\"). |\n| **DEF-03** | Canvas Node Hover \u0026 Interaction Stability (`functional_specification_006.md` Section 3, Section 4.3.1-4.3.3, Acceptance Criteria 3) | In `GraphCanvas.tsx`: hover handler calls `setHoveredNode(hovered)`, updating React state. This causes `render` callback to be recreated (line 310 dependency `hoveredNode`). The simulation `useEffect` at line 348 depends on `[nodes, links, render]`. | Every hover event tears down the D3 simulation (`simulation.stop()`) and restarts a brand new simulation with `alpha = 1` and `-120` repulsive charge. This violently displaces nodes away from the cursor in an infinite jitter loop, making click selection evasive and frustrating. |\n| **DEF-04** | Autonomous Stabilization Upon Load (`functional_specification_006.md` Section 4.1.2) | The simulation in `GraphCanvas.tsx` lines 322-348 restarts repeatedly whenever state changes (`render` dependency), preventing autonomous stabilization. | The graph layout never settles into a quiescent, stable state if user cursor moves across nodes. |\n| **DEF-05** | CMS MCD \"Invalid Article Version\" Failure Elimination (`functional_specification_006.md` Section 3, Section 4.4.1, Acceptance Criteria 4) | `NodeDetailDrawer.tsx` line 72 hardcodes `https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=59508`. Programmatic probe confirms this redirects to `search.aspx?error=Invalid%20Article%20Version`. | Users clicking the coverage policy source link arrive at an error screen rather than active documentation. |\n| **DEF-06** | CMS Change Request Dead Link Elimination (`functional_specification_006.md` Section 4.4.6, Acceptance Criteria 4) | `NodeDetailDrawer.tsx` line 77 hardcodes `https://www.cms.gov/files/document/r13286cp.pdf`. Programmatic HTTP probe returns `HTTP/2 404 Not Found`. | Clicking the Change Request link produces a dead 404 page. |\n| **DEF-07** | Missing External Government Links for Multiple Entity Types (`functional_specification_006.md` Section 4.4.7-4.4.9, Acceptance Criteria 4) | `NodeDetailDrawer.tsx` `getGovernmentSourceLink()` has no cases for `Jurisdiction`, `HCPCSCode`, or `ICD10Code`, falling through to `default: return null;`. | When inspecting regional contractors (e.g. CGS or Noridian), procedure codes (A6522), or diagnosis codes (I97.2), zero external source link is rendered in the drawer. |\n| **DEF-08** | Dynamic Property-Driven URL Parameterization (`functional_specification_006.md` Section 3, Section 4.4.2-4.4.4, Section 4.4.10) | `NodeDetailDrawer.tsx` hardcodes static URLs for `Bill` (always H.R. 3630), `PublicLaw` (always 117-328), `Regulation` (hardcoded date string), and `LobbyingFiling` (generic search homepage). | Selecting H.R. 2617 or H.R. 3808 displays an incorrect link pointing to H.R. 3630. Selecting lobbying filing `c8697fc5-...` links to generic search instead of specific disclosure document. |\n| **DEF-09** | Frontend Verification and Test Suite Coverage (`functional_specification_006.md` Section 5 Acceptance Criteria 1-4) | Current automated test suites test backend logic and REST endpoints only. Zero automated component tests verify frontend toolbar cleanliness, HUD accordion toggle, stationary hover stability, or link generation logic. | Acceptance criteria cannot be programmatically validated without dedicated frontend component and link audit tests. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Sufficiency \u0026 Scan Certification\n\nIn strict accordance with the evaluation parameters in [`LANGUAGE.md`](file:///Users/diesel/Desktop/LAG/.sandcastle/worktrees/agent-plan-scan-1-20261013T165618-008-wcap/LANGUAGE.md):\n\n- **`{sufficient}` Certification:** The static scan of the codebase and active read-only reconnaissance of external datasources are co